  "notes": "Warm cream page (#f6f2ea) with a deep forest-green sidebar and primary buttons; red-tinted surfaces mark the one blocking problem (Unassigned tile, warning alert, blocked option), amber marks the affected row and the dishwasher's bar. The copy explains things in plain language using the user's real figures. Choosing a radio option switches the preview panel to 'Previewing' with +$ diff amounts per person and a green 'Balanced to the cent' bar (checked live). The disabled third option shows its consequence ('$171.20 over the 20% limit') to explain why it is blocked. The clock-out chart is a small custom timeline: hatched bar for the excluded manager, diamonds for late checks, dashed line at the last server's clock-out. Step 3 contains nested per-shift disclosure rows and an inline add-declaration form, seen only in the live page."
